  {
   "id": "theme-pre-training-and-how-it-was-reused",
   "name": "Pre-training and how it was reused",
   "summary": "Sets out the practice BERT builds on: train a model on unlabeled text once, then reuse it on a labeled task that has far less data. The paper sorts prior work into two strategies. One keeps the pre-trained model frozen and feeds its vectors into a hand-built architecture as extra features; the other adds a small head and fine-tunes every pre-trained weight. ELMo is the paper's example of the first and OpenAI GPT of the second, and BERT is defined against both, so this comes first.",
