  {
   "id": "theme-one-architecture-two-stages",
   "name": "One architecture, two stages",
   "summary": "BERT is one Transformer encoder used twice: pre-trained on unlabeled text, then fine-tuned on a labeled task from those weights. Fine-tuning yields a separate model per task, but the paper stresses that the network barely changes between the two stages. This theme also fixes the size shorthand — L layers, hidden size H, A attention heads — and the two reported configurations, 110M parameters for BERT_BASE and 340M for BERT_LARGE. BERT_BASE was sized to match OpenAI GPT so the later comparison turns on bidirectionality rather than capacity.",
