  {
   "id": "theme-what-bert-reads",
   "name": "What BERT reads",
   "summary": "One input format has to cover a single text, a sentence pair and a question with its passage. A sequence opens with [CLS], packs one or two spans separated by [SEP], and gives every token a vector that is the sum of three learned embeddings: which token it is, which of the two spans it sits in, and which position it occupies. Two outputs are named here because everything later reads them: C, the final vector at [CLS], and T_i, the final vector at token i. Read this before the pre-training tasks, which are defined over exactly these positions.",
