  {
   "id": "theme-the-two-pre-training-tasks",
   "name": "The two pre-training tasks",
   "summary": "The two self-supervised objectives, and the run that trained them. Masked LM hides 15% of the tokens and predicts them from both sides, which gets around the fact that a bidirectional model would otherwise reach the token it is predicting through the layers below. Next sentence prediction asks, from the [CLS] vector, whether span B really followed span A in the corpus. The rest is the recipe: 3.3 billion words of books and Wikipedia, one million steps, and a schedule that saves the long sequences for the final tenth of training.",
