   "id": "theme-adapting-to-a-task",
   "name": "Adapting to a task",
   "summary": "How a pre-trained BERT becomes a task model. The task's texts are mapped onto the A and B slots — a single text uses an empty second slot — and one output layer is attached to either C or the per-token vectors. Every parameter is then trained on the labeled data, which the paper says costs at most an hour on one Cloud TPU. The hyperparameter grid is small enough to run in full, though the authors report that small datasets are far more sensitive to the choice than large ones.",
