  {
   "id": "theme-taking-pieces-away",
   "name": "Taking pieces away",
   "summary": "The experiments that remove or vary one piece of BERT at a time, to see what each is worth. Two cut-down pre-training runs charge a score drop to next sentence prediction and then to bidirectionality separately. A size ladder from 3 layers up to 24 finds that larger is better on every task tested, including the small ones, which the paper explains only as a hypothesis about how few fresh parameters fine-tuning adds. Two further ablations ask whether the full million steps are needed and whether the 80/10/10 masking mixture matters, the second run both fine-tuned and with BERT frozen on CoNLL-2003 NER.",
